      "evidenceText": "MuckRock We give you the tools to keep government transparent and accountable MuckRock Foundation is a nonprofit, collaborative organization and newsroom that brings together journalists, researchers and the public to request, analyze and share government information, making politics more transparent and democracy more informed. Donate Shop merch Subscribe to the newsletter Learn more about our mission and impact File, track and share public records requests File a request Search requests Learn how it works 188,970 filed requests 29,553 agencies 63,183 fulfilled requests 12,529,216 pages released Analyze, annotate and publish primary source documents Upload a document Search public documents Learn how it works 7,550,965 public documents 126,325,991 public pages 550,645 public notes An initiative to identify, obtain, reformat, clean, document, publish and disseminate government datasets of public interest Get involved Search datasets Learn how it works 1,169 participants 24 total datasets Multiply your newsroom's investigative impact with a Sunlight Research Desk Membership Our research experts help newsrooms dig deeper to produce stories with impact. Sunlight Research Desk's exclusive membership options give your team the resources they need. Whether you're backgrounding a source, tracking campaign money, or connecting the dots in public records — we're the support system behind the byline . Explore our plans and become a member For the Record Keep up on new releases, projects and reporting with MuckRock's weekly newsletter Subscribe with your email address Subscribe By subscribing, you agree to MuckRock's Terms of Service and Privacy Policy . The impact of anti-trans federal action Police disciplinary files ‘The Air We Breathe:’ How industry is polluting Cicero’s air The impact of anti-trans federal action  &rarr; The Trans Journalists Association and MuckRock have partnered to help journalists document and report on the Trump administration’s actions targeting trans communities. We’re going beyond the initial headlines to uncover and preserve newsworthy documents and data that reveal the real-world effects of anti-trans policies. This open-source project will track the implementation and practical effects of executive orders, legislation and other federal action. We have records for health and education reporters (or anyone, really) March 31, 2026 by Ileana Garnand Ringing in the new year with records requests January 26, 2026 by Ileana Garnand We’re requesting ICE documents on transgender detainees December 17, 2025 by Ileana Garnand TJA and MuckRock's collaboration hit 300 records requests. Here's what we got back. November 26, 2025 by Ileana Garnand Police disciplinary files  &rarr; We want to free up police disciplinary files in more places across the country, make them open for all and highlight the work of others doing the same. Five ways to use Brady lists to investigate police misconduct April 29, 2026 by Lily Dokhanchi and Jasmine Lewin How to investigate police misconduct using Brady lists and public records April 15, 2026 by Jasmine Lewin and Lily Dokhanchi A requester’s guide to police misconduct documents and data March 25, 2026 by Lily Dokhanchi, Dillon Bergin and Jasmine Lewin These agencies withheld police disciplinary files. Help us challenge that. September 4, 2025 by Dillon Bergin ‘The Air We Breathe:’ How industry is polluting Cicero’s air  &rarr; \"The Air We Breathe\" is a yearlong investigative project by two nonprofit newsrooms, the Cicero Independiente and MuckRock, who have been monitoring air pollution in Cicero. What we found: Cicero’s air quality is much worse than surrounding Cook County neighborhoods, and it’s worse than what the Environmental Protection Agency and pilot programs run by the city and Microsoft have routinely reported. Elected officials are opting out of secret Koppers community meetings about air pollution. July 8, 2024 by Derek Kravitz The inside story on a billion-dollar chemical company’s fight to keep its secrets from the public April 8, 2024 by Derek Kravitz, Jorge Martinez and Dillon Bergin FOIAFriday A community podcast about all things FOIA and public records We gather once a month to share updates on public records laws and rulings, techniques, tricks and insider tips from fellow requesters. Learn more about FOIAFriday Join our next FOIAFriday session Explore the FOIAFriday archive on YouTube Investigating with Sunlight Your go-to resource for investigative work Hosted by the Sunlight Research Desk, this monthly training series covers a wide range of investigative research and reporting topics. Come to learn, share your work, and connect with a community of investigators at every level. Learn more about Investigating with Sunlight Join our upcoming sessions Dive into Sunlight Research Desk's Resources Join Sunlight Research Desk's Community Office Hours Explore the Investigating with Sunlight archive on YouTube Building with MuckRock Get more out of every tool Hosted by our tech team, this monthly series is your space to dive deep into DocumentCloud, discover the latest platform updates, and ask any questions along the way. Whether you're a first-time user or an experienced developer, come ready to build. Learn more about Building with MuckRock Join our next Building with MuckRock workshop Explore the Building with MuckRock archive on YouTube Training to Fit Your Needs Custom training built around you Not every organization has the same needs, so why settle for a one-size-fits-all training? Contact us to build a custom session tailored to your team, explore our training menu to find the right fit, or sign up for one of our onboarding sessions for MuckRock Requests or DocumentCloud. Learn about private trainings Explore our Training Menu Contact us to learn more",
